<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place</p><h1 class="enc-title">Aztlan</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Aztlan is the legendary <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bantustan">homeland</a> from which the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexica">Mexica</a> (<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aztec-empire">Aztecs</a>) and other <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nahuas">Nahua</a> peoples were said to have migrated to central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a>. Their accounts describe it as an island in a lake somewhere to the north, which the Mexica left in the 12th century, wandering for generations before founding <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tenochtitlan">Tenochtitlan</a>. Its location, if it existed, is unknown, and it has become a symbol of origin in Mexican and Chicano culture.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/aztlan.jpg" alt="Aztlan" width="320" height="237" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Gemelli Careri · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gemelli_Careri_Aztec_Map.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
